differential2 §12c. The comprehension loop-lowering now covers an
iterable that is a call/expression yielding a runtime (non-constant-
length) list, not just a list parameter; set comprehensions share the
list lowering, so they benefit too. Literal/range/constant-length
iterables still take the unroll path.
